# Your Issue

Issue: demo#ab12 - Fix the # crash now
Run `kata show demo#ab12` for its body, comments and attachments before you start.

# Contract

- Claim it first: `kata claim demo#ab12 --ttl 24h`. If another actor owns the Issue, stop and ask the user; don't take it. If you already own it (a todo plan may have claimed it for you without a TTL), run the same command again: it renews the claim with the TTL.
- Comment what you did and how you checked it: `kata comment demo#ab12 -m "<what you did and how you verified it>"`.
- Only when the work is done and verified, close the Issue with evidence: `kata close demo#ab12 --done -m "<what was done and how it was verified>"` plus `--commit <sha>`, `--pr <url>`, `--test "<command>"` or `--reviewed <path>`. Otherwise leave it open. Never pad or invent evidence.
- Finish or drop the open todo child Issues under it before you close it; open children block the close.
- When you need a decision, ask the user and wait for the answer.
- If you stop without closing the Issue, hand it to a human in this order: comment why; `kata meta set demo#ab12 work.attention needs-human`; `kata meta set demo#ab12 work.attention_msg "<why>"`; then `kata label rm demo#ab12 ready-for-agent` (when it has that label) and `kata label add demo#ab12 ready-for-human`.
